 {"id": "ko-0455", "verdict": "rewrite", "category": "contrastive-trap", "focus": "푹 (puk) is the go-to intensifier for 쉬다/자다 (rest up, sleep soundly) – but 'only with rest or sleep' overclaims (푹 삶다, 푹 빠지다 exist); restate the collocation without the false exclusivity."},
 {"id": "ko-0456", "verdict": "rewrite", "category": "contrastive-trap", "focus": "The real rule is which time words take 에: 내년에 (naenyeone) does, while 오늘/내일/어제 drop it – 'future time words still take 에' as written misleads, since 내일 normally takes no 에."},
 {"id": "ko-0460", "verdict": "drop", "category": "vocab-gloss"},
