 {"id": "ko-0476", "verdict": "rewrite", "category": "contrastive-trap", "focus": "새 (sae) works only before a noun – you cannot say a thing 'is 새'; the predicate needs 새로워요 (saerowoyo). The placement fact alone is trivial; the attributive-only trap is the earned insight."},
